  "title": "Erdős Problem #616",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $r\\geq 3$. For an $r$-uniform hypergraph $G$ let $\\tau(G)$ denote the covering number (or transversal number), the minimum size of a set of vertices which includes at least one from each edge in $G$.\nDetermine the best possible $t$ such that, if $G$ is an $r$-uniform hypergraph $G$ where every subgraph $G'$ on at most $3r-3$ vertices has $\\tau(G')\\leq 1$, we have $\\tau(G)\\leq t$.",
